 Operational CLI diagnostics belong on stderr. Evidence and coverage diagnostics remain fields in the single JSON or SARIF document on stdout. Preserve nonzero exit codes and incomplete coverage when deciding whether a result is usable.
+
+## OntologyEngineering integration (project-maintained addition)
+
+When this tool is used within OntologyEngineering, resolve `ONTOLOGY_ENGINEERING_ROOT`
+from the user's configuration and read `docs/TOOL-INTEGRATIONS.md` and
+`references/professional-capabilities.md` under that root. Keep the current Project,
+object revision, conditions and pending decision; do not infer a Project from cwd.
+Save the exact invocation, tool version, original result bytes, input identities,
+coverage, failures and unknowns in the Project's private evidence directory.
+Return results through `oev2 project tool-result`; registration does not grant
+engineering adoption. Feed actual process and usage back through `oev2 memory`.
+Do not require an additional hosted judgment service for this handoff.
+
+Keep static candidates, theoretical estimates, imported measurements and behavior checks separate. A candidate is not a measured bottleneck or an adopted optimization.
+
+This addition is maintained by OntologyEngineering, not by the upstream tool.
+Apply it only to the version and original Skill hash in `integrations/tools.lock.json`.
+An upstream setup or upgrade may replace the Skill; re-check before reapplying.
